OL,3,GNEWSAThe man who vowed to stop
OL,4,A'inhumane treatment of climbing boys'
OL,5,
OL,6,FA social reformer who relentlessly
OL,7,Fcampaigned against the inhumane
OL,8,Fpractice of using child chimney sweeps
OL,9,Fhas been honoured with a blue plaque
OL,10,Foutside his former home.
OL,12,FWilliam Wood, who was born in 1782, was
OL,13,Fa successful wool merchant before
OL,14,Fbecoming one of Britain's most
OL,15,Fdetermined social reformers.
OL,17,FHis campaigning laid the groundwork for
OL,18,Fthe Chimney Sweepers Act of 1875, which
OL,19,Ffinally banned the practice, but Wood
OL,20,Fdid not live to see the law enacted as
OL,21,Fhe died in 1868 at the age of 85.
OL,23,APub: 20-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NW Eng NewsC Reg TVF Weather
